## Rows skipped

nb-a 2 P1 — 004 link label «artikkel 10 i næringsavgiftsloven» on pcode=G0340028&flno=3. Not applied. See reviewer-wrong below. URL and the digit 10 unchanged.

nb-a 13 P2 and nb-b 20 P2 — space as thousands separator («500 000», «1 579 589»). Skipped. ACCEPTED-ROUND forbids space thousands; scripts/check-column-translation.mjs sets NUMBER_THOUSAND_STYLE.nb to 'dot'. Column amounts stay 500.000 / 1.579.589 / 3.000.000 and the rest. The guidance bio’s existing «1 570 000» was left as it was.

nb-a 15 P2 and nb-b 25 P2 — delete U+200B, drop 005’s empty bold lines, and turn 003 Q16–Q20 into ## headings. Skipped. The checker requires the same ZWSP count as the Korean source (003: 52, 005: 8 including 4 bold-only lines, 006: 4, 008: 10, 009: 5, 013: 5, 015: 3) and the same heading levels. Removing the characters or adding headings fails blocks/headings. 005 and 009 had no other row.

nb-a 14 P2, the other glued «1»s — «mer enn 1 utenlandsk statsborger» (005), «på 1 navn» (007), «fullførte 1 års» and «per 1 år» (008). Digits not removed. The Korean source counts them (1명 / 1건 / 1년 / 1인), and a missing 1 fails the number check. «en/et» is not in the nb number lexicon unless it is tied to a listed unit, so writing the digit out as a word would not replace it. Those phrases were already grammatical. Only the ungrammatical 003 formula was rephrased, with both 1s kept.

